    <item>
      <title>Optimal swine nutrition: don’t feed more, but feed better</title>
      <link>https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/animals/pigs/optimal-swine-nutrition-dont-feed-more-but-feed-better/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=optimal-swine-nutrition-dont-feed-more-but-feed-better</link>
      <description>A one-size-fits-all diet for pigs can lead to overfeeding or underfeeding, producing varying results, and lost production. Instead, JD Mostert, independent swine nutritionist, advocates for a stronger focus on digestible amino acids to get the most from feed rations.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/animals/pigs/optimal-swine-nutrition-dont-feed-more-but-feed-better/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=optimal-swine-nutrition-dont-feed-more-but-feed-better</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://cax-wp-farmers-prod-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/app/uploads/2026/02/Weaner-piglets.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Feb 2026 03:00:36 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
