      <title>FMD suspected in Humansdorp amid worsening drought</title>
      <link>https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/agri-news/south-africa/fmd-suspected-in-humansdorp-amid-worsening-drought/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=fmd-suspected-in-humansdorp-amid-worsening-drought</link>
      <description>Farmers in Humansdorp, Eastern Cape, face a suspected foot-and-mouth disease outbreak amid one of the worst droughts the area has seen in decades, with more than 100 cattle possibly affected. Officials warn urgent, coordinated action is needed to avoid catastrophic livestock losses.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/agri-news/south-africa/fmd-suspected-in-humansdorp-amid-worsening-drought/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=fmd-suspected-in-humansdorp-amid-worsening-drought</guid>
